I'm just saying rough
pseudocode here.

00:49:30.680 --> 00:49:32.240
Dot is convex.

00:49:32.240 --> 00:49:33.980
Well, there's only
one in that list

00:49:33.980 --> 00:49:35.660
and it would return
this function.

00:49:35.660 --> 00:49:38.030
And that would evaluate to what?

00:49:38.030 --> 00:49:38.900
False.

00:49:38.900 --> 00:49:41.180
At that point, it's game over.

00:49:41.180 --> 00:49:43.610
But if you want it to be
really sure it was over,

00:49:43.610 --> 00:49:46.250
you would actually go to the
equality constraints and it

00:49:46.250 --> 00:49:47.750
would have my--

00:49:47.750 --> 00:49:50.430
it would actually do-- it'd
be for equality constraints.

00:49:50.430 --> 00:49:54.650
And for equality constraint,
inequality constraints

00:49:54.650 --> 00:50:00.320
equality, my prob dot equality
constraint function of 0 zero,

00:50:00.320 --> 00:50:02.930
I'm using zero
indexing, dot is affine

00:50:02.930 --> 00:50:04.850
and it would evaluate to false.

00:50:04.850 --> 00:50:06.680
Everybody got this?

00:50:06.680 --> 00:50:09.690
Now, it's silly because you look
at this and you're like, well,

00:50:09.690 --> 00:50:10.900
this is dumb.

00:50:10.900 --> 00:50:12.510
I mean, this thing
is the same as x1

00:50:12.510 --> 00:50:14.250
just being less than
or equal to zero.

00:50:14.250 --> 00:50:18.460
And the square of x1 plus x2
is zero, that only happens--

00:50:18.460 --> 00:50:21.390
so basically, you can
rewrite the problem this way.

00:50:21.390 --> 00:50:24.090
Now, what we do is we would call
this problem and this problem

00:50:24.090 --> 00:50:25.920
equivalent problems.

00:50:25.920 --> 00:50:29.100
What that means is,
if you can solve one,

00:50:29.100 --> 00:50:30.760
there's an easy way
to solve the other.

00:50:30.760 --> 00:50:31.885
We'll talk more about that.

00:50:31.885 --> 00:50:34.590
But if you've taken a
course in computer science,

00:50:34.590 --> 00:50:38.730
almost any, this is the
standard idea of a reduction.

00:50:38.730 --> 00:50:41.635
We're not going to make it fancy
and have polynomial reduction

00:50:41.635 --> 00:50:42.760
and all that kind of stuff.

00:50:42.760 --> 00:50:44.927
But the point is, for us,
it's going to be informal.

00:50:44.927 --> 00:50:47.250
It just means two
problems are equivalent.

00:50:47.250 --> 00:50:50.040
When I solve one, I know
how to solve the other.

00:50:50.040 --> 00:50:51.540
And if I can solve
the other, I know

00:50:51.540 --> 00:50:53.310
how to solve the original one.

00:50:53.310 --> 00:50:56.890
So these are equivalent;
they are not the same.

00:50:56.890 --> 00:50:59.290
Let's walk through
the implementation.

00:50:59.290 --> 00:51:03.390
This is my prob, and this
is my alternative prob.

00:51:03.390 --> 00:51:06.630
So let's walk through the
equals equals method between two

00:51:06.630 --> 00:51:08.970
problems, and the way
that works is this.

00:51:08.970 --> 00:51:10.780
Here's an implementation.

00:51:10.780 --> 00:51:12.540
This is what it
means to be equal.

00:51:12.540 --> 00:51:15.720
It says, are your
objectives equal?

00:51:15.720 --> 00:51:19.630
And that would evaluate
to what in this case?

00:51:19.630 --> 00:51:21.490
True.

00:51:21.490 --> 00:51:22.900
Then, it goes like this.

00:51:22.900 --> 00:51:27.280
It's really dumb it says, loop
over the constraints and just

00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:31.510
check if each constraint
function in the two problems

00:51:31.510 --> 00:51:32.440
are the same.

00:51:32.440 --> 00:51:36.890
That would evaluate
here to false.

00:51:36.890 --> 00:51:38.990
So these are not
the same problem,

00:51:38.990 --> 00:51:41.777
but they are equivalent.

00:51:41.777 --> 00:51:44.360
I mean, this is not a big deal
and it should be kept informal,

00:51:44.360 --> 00:51:47.090
but it's also an important idea.

00:51:47.090 --> 00:51:50.150
So this problem is not
convex, this is convex.

00:51:50.150 --> 00:51:53.210
And this tells you that
yes, a non-convex problem

00:51:53.210 --> 00:51:55.670
can be equivalent
to a convex problem,

00:51:55.670 --> 00:51:58.010
and that's very
confusing, but too bad.

00:52:02.668 --> 00:52:04.210
Would that be the
same as just saying

00:52:04.210 --> 00:52:06.850
that the star that
solves this problem

00:52:06.850 --> 00:52:09.340
is the same as the star that
will solve that problem?

00:52:09.340 --> 00:52:12.970
Would that be another way
to check equivalence of it.

